 "result_text": "Creating a PR (a `POST` to `/pulls`) needs a token even on a public repo. Reading `/pulls` doesn't, which is why it works in the browser. Without a token, GitHub answers the write with a 404 instead of a 401. The old message blamed an \"expired token\" and never said the token might be missing.\n\nI changed the 404 handler in `git_machete/github.py` so the message depends on whether a token was found:\n- **No token:** it says the endpoint doesn't exist or requires authentication, and lists where to provide a `repo`-scoped token, with the token-generation link.\n- **Token present:** it says the token may be invalid, expired, or lack `repo` access.\n\nI also fixed the 401/403 message, which printed a malformed URL (`https://https://api.github.com...`). It now prints the real URL.\n\nI haven't run the tests or the command against GitHub.",
